Extract EVERY purchased line item from this receipt or payment slip (Thai and/or English). Return ONLY valid JSON, no markdown:
{"is_receipt":true,"date":"YYYY-MM-DD","time":"HH:MM","vendor":"","total":0,"tax":0,"currency":"THB","reference_no":"","confidence":0.0,"category":"food|transport|shopping|utilities|health|other","items":[{"name":"","qty":1,"amount":0,"category":"food|transport|shopping|utilities|health|other"}]}
Rules: one object in items per line on the receipt; amount = line total (qty x unit price); skip subtotal, VAT, discount, change and payment lines; for a bank transfer slip use ONE item named after the recipient with the transferred amount; use null if unreadable; convert Buddhist Era years (พ.ศ.) to Christian Era by subtracting 543; Thai receipts often print a 2-digit year, e.g. 06/10/69 means 2569 BE = 2026-10-06. reference_no = the transaction/reference number printed on a bank slip, or the receipt/invoice number; copy it EXACTLY, keeping upper/lower case; null if none is printed. confidence = 0 to 1, how sure you are that date, total and vendor were read correctly. If the image is not a receipt, bill, invoice or payment slip, or nothing on it is readable, return {"date":null,"vendor":null,"total":0,"items":[]} - never invent vendors, items or amounts. Set is_receipt to false (and items to []) for photos of people, places, screenshots, blank or unreadable images - only true when you can actually read a store/recipient name or amounts on it.

